<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Point the Surface planet layer's backgroundBiome at our own water.

    🔑 `PlanetLayerDef.backgroundBiome` is referenced in ONE place in the whole 1.6
    codebase — WorldDrawLayer_Terrain.cs:48 — so this changes the colour of the
    water inside Peninsula / Bay / CoastalIsland masks and NOTHING ELSE. It does
    not touch the sea, the shader, elevation, or any biome a tile actually has.

    ⚠️ Do not confuse `PlanetLayerDef.backgroundBiome` (a BiomeDef reference, this
    file) with `BiomeDef.isBackgroundBiome` (a bool, used by LandmarkDef.IsValidTile
    to decide which neighbours count as water for landmark rotation). Different
    fields, similar names, unrelated jobs.

    Deliberately NOT wrapped in a Conditional: Surface is a Core def and cannot be
    absent. If Ludeon ever renames it we want the red error, because the silent
    failure is capes going black again and nobody noticing for weeks.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/PlanetLayerDef[defName="Surface"]/backgroundBiome</xpath>
    <value><backgroundBiome>Jawa_BackgroundWater</backgroundBiome></value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
